# Irissakuya content workflow

## Source of truth

- User-authored content lives in `content/` only.
- Generated/presentation HTML lives in `about/`, `journal/`, `skills/`, `achievements/`, `index.html`.
- Never ask the user to hand-edit HTML for routine content updates.

## Directory layout

```
content/
  about.yaml
  skills.yaml
  achievements.yaml
  journal/YYYY-MM-DD-slug.md
assets/images/          ← article images
journal/posts/slug.html ← generated articles
```

## Formats

- **Journal**: Markdown + YAML frontmatter (`title`, `date`, `category`, `description`, `draft`, `featured`, `tags`). Categories: `notes` | `research` | `life`.
- **About / Skills / Achievements**: YAML (see `content/README.md` for schemas).
- Filenames: `YYYY-MM-DD-slug.md`; slug becomes URL under `journal/posts/`.

## Agent duties when publishing

1. Read or receive content in the formats above.
2. Generate or update HTML using existing classes in `assets/page.css` (`.elegant-list`, `.card`, `.list-item`, etc.).
3. Update list pages (`journal/index.html`), hide empty state when entries exist, sync `updateCount()` data.
4. Optionally surface latest or `featured` posts on `index.html`.
5. Keep site UI in English unless the user explicitly requests Chinese content.

## User commands (act on these)

- “发布 `content/journal/…md`” → generate post HTML + update lists.
- “把下面加到 About …” → update `content/about.yaml` + `about/index.html`.
- “更新 skills/achievements …” → update YAML + matching page.

## Do not

- Use Word/PDF/Notion export as source without converting to Markdown/YAML first.
- Duplicate content in both `content/` and HTML without syncing.
- Break existing banner themes, nav, or Live2D setup when adding pages.

Full templates and examples: `content/README.md`.
